{title: I Will Pour Out My Heart}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
(verse)

Verse 2
Here in your presence today
My heart pledging only to you
From now til eternity comes
I promise my love to be true.

Verse 3
As Y'shua gave all for His bride
As He loved her in measure unknown
And gave up His life
Sparing nothing to make her His own...
His very own.

Verse 4
(refrain)
I will pour out my heart to you
As He poured out His life for me.
Consecrated with you in love,
Set apart we will be

Verse 5
I'm preparing a place in my heart
As He's preparing a dwelling above.
And together we'll find,
One in spirit and mind,
The fullness of heaven-sent love...

Verse 6
(musical interlude)

Verse 7
As we join in betrothal today
Lord Y'shua stands here by our side
His promise is sure
That forever with us He'll abide...
He will abide.

Verse 8
(refrain)
I will pour out my heart to you
As He poured out His life for me.
Consecrated with you in love,
Set apart we will be

Verse 9
I'm preparing a place in my heart
As He's preparing a dwelling above.
And together we'll find,
One in spirit and mind,
The fullness of heaven-sent love

Verse 10
(Bridge)
I will pour out my heart,
Not sparing the cost,
As Y'shua gave all in redeeming the lost.
I am pledging my heart, He is my witness, to you
Til eternity comes,
I will pour out my heart
To you!

Verse 11
(refrain)
I will pour out my heart to you
As He poured out His life for me.
Consecrated with you in love,
Set apart we will be

Verse 12
I'm preparing a place in my heart
As He's preparing a dwelling above.
And together we'll find,
One in spirit and mind,
The fullness of heaven-sent love

Verse 13
And together we'll find,
One in spirit and mind,
The fullness of heaven-sent love!
